From 657cde6342357029c2e77381ab302617a94fb6ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:02:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wmaker: keep the Dock visible when it changes monitor, and a
 way to bring it back

Choosing a monitor in the Dock menu kept the side the Dock was on: on
the leftmost monitor of three the Dock went to its right edge, the seam
between two monitors, where it is kept below the windows of that
monitor ("Normal" level) and the pointer goes past it into the next
monitor. For the user it disappeared.

- When the monitor is chosen, the Dock goes to the side of that monitor
  that is an edge of the whole screen and is not taken by the Clip;
  if none is, a side free of the Clip; otherwise it keeps its side.
- After the move the Dock is checked to be inside a monitor (if not, it
  is moved as below) and brought in front once, so it is seen where it
  went; the choice is saved only then.
- "Restore Dock position" (Monitor submenu of the Dock, RESET_DOCK in
  the root menu, and the _WINDOWMAKER_COMMAND "ResetDock" sent by
  big-wm-dock-reset when no menu can be reached): primary monitor,
  right side unless the Clip is there, top, in front of the windows.
  The applications, dockapps, drawers and level of the Dock are kept.
- wDockUpdateHead (RandR changes, restore) also falls back to that when
  the Dock would end outside every monitor.

Tested in Xephyr with three Xinerama heads (800, 900 and 700 px): each
monitor chosen from the menu, a saved monitor that does not exist,
"ResetDock" from the command line, and the Dock with wmnet and
wmcpuload docked moving between monitors, all checked on screenshots.
